@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: what proveo clean reclaims, what it refuses to touch, and the liveness gate in front of it
' covers: internal/clean/**
' covers: cmd/proveo/clean.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/clean_legacy_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/clean_run_state_test.go
'
' 2026-10-16: the docker+egress backend is DELETED, so nothing creates an
' egress session container, an egress network or broker.env any more. The
' per-run state dir holds the sbx Kit, the policy log and the run's other
' artifacts; an older run's dir may still hold a broker.env.
'
' ONE RUN ROOT AFTER v0.2.0 (N13 retirement completed).
' A run writes <stateDir>/runs/<sid> (run.RunDirOf). RunRoots() returns only
' <stateDir>/runs. stateSessions() lists its session ids; runClean removes
' their state directories. The retired <stateDir>/egress root was swept for
' one release and is no longer scanned or deleted. Test:
' TestCleanSweepsRunStateUnderRunsOnly (cmd/proveo/clean_run_state_test.go).
'
' ONE LEGACY SWEEP (F11, DONE (wt) 2026-10-17; the user: "One legacy sweep
' (Recommended)"). MEASURED: cmd/proveo/clean.go gatherLegacyDocker (:170-200)
' gathers everything the retired docker backend could leave — egress containers
' and networks (`label=proveo.egress.session`), `proveo-dind-*` containers, and
' `docker volume ls --filter name=proveo-squid-cache-` volumes — and runClean
' removes the volumes with `docker volume rm`. internal/clean carries them as
' Inventory.Volumes / Plan.Volumes; BuildPlan holds every volume back (reported
' as "volume <name>" in SkippedLive) while ANY egress container still runs,
' unless --force (clean.go:88-98). Tests: TestBuildPlanSweepsTheRetiredBackendsSquidVolumes
' (internal/clean/clean_test.go) and TestTheLegacySweepFindsEveryRetiredDockerLeftover
' (cmd/proveo/clean_legacy_test.go, a fake docker). "Delete the sweep in a later
' release" is recorded, not scheduled.
'
' A STATE DIR IS LIVE WHEN ITS PROCESS IS. With no egress container to stand for
' a run, a running container can no longer mark an sbx session live. MEASURED:
' cmd/proveo/clean.go sessionAlive(sid) parses the pid out of the session id
' (proveo-<unix>-<pid>) and probes it with os.FindProcess + Signal(0); a live
' one lands in Inventory.LiveSessions, and internal/clean keeps that state dir.
' [Inference] A pid reused by an unrelated process reads as live — the safe
' direction: a dir kept, never a live run's dir removed.
title `proveo clean` — reclaim leaked run state without killing live runs

actor "Maintainer" as MT

node "Host" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "cmd/proveo clean\ngathers inventory · executes plan" as CMD <<app>>
  component "internal/clean\nBuildPlan(inv, opts) — pure" as CORE <<app>>

  frame "Inventory" as INV <<host>> {
    component "LEGACY egress session containers\n(mitm · squid · ollama — none created since 2026-10-16)" as C <<app>>
    component "legacy DinD sidecars\n(retired; never session-labeled)" as D <<app>>
    component "LEGACY egress networks\n+ HasEndpoints" as N <<app>>
    database "LEGACY proveo-squid-cache-* volumes\n(held back while an egress container runs)" as VOL <<db>>
    database "<stateDir>/runs/<sid>\nsbx Kit · policy log" as ST <<error>>
    database "proveo/* images" as IMG <<db>>
    database "PROVEO_HOME (~/.proveo)\nsessions + seeded config" as PH <<db>>
    database "provisioned toolchains\n""toolchains/<os>-<arch>/"" per platform\n""\.local/share/mise"" · ""\.go"" · ""go"" · shims" as TOOLS <<db>>
  }
}

MT ARROW_MAIN CMD
CMD ARROW_MAIN CORE : Inventory + Options
CORE ARROW_MAIN CMD : Plan{remove…, SkippedLive}

CORE ARROW_MAIN C : routine — dead sessions only
CORE ARROW_MAIN D : routine
CORE ARROW_MAIN N : routine — only when no endpoints
CORE ARROW_MAIN VOL : routine — none while an egress container runs\n(unless ""--force"")
CORE ARROW_ERROR ST : routine — successLabel(wipes broker.env)
CORE ARROW_OPTIONAL IMG : ""--deep"" only
CORE ARROW_OPTIONAL PH : ""--homes"" only
CORE ARROW_OPTIONAL TOOLS : ""--tools"" only

note bottom of TOOLS
  **A cache, held to a stricter liveness rule than everything else.** The
  toolchain tree is what makes install-once/run-many work: language servers, the
  Go toolchain and the jdtls JDK land under PROVEO_HOME, so a warm run installs
  nothing. Nothing else prunes it, and it only grows.

  **One tree per platform, plus the legacy one.** ""_proveo_tool_home"" writes to
  ""PROVEO_HOME/toolchains/<os>-<arch>"" so the docker backend (deleted
  2026-10-16) and the sbx VM could SHARE a tree without an amd64 install answering ""command -v"" for an arm64
  sandbox. ""toolRoots"" globs those and keeps PROVEO_HOME itself in the list:
  trees installed before the relocation are still on operators' disks, and a
  flag that silently stopped reclaiming them would be worse than the growth.

  Per-session ephemera belong to exactly one run, so liveness is decided per
  session. This tree is shared by every run on the machine, so ANY running
  proveo container **or sbx sandbox** holds the whole prune back — ""--force"" is
  the documented escape hatch. The sandbox arm is not symmetry: an sbx run has
  no egress sidecar and no dind, so counting only containers read "nothing is
  running" on that backend every time — while an sbx run copies its toolchains
  into this very tree at teardown. A prune racing that copy leaves the store half
  written, which is the worst outcome available: a tree that satisfies
  ""command -v"" on the next run and fails on first exec. An unreadable ""sbx ls""
  is undecidable, not quiet, and holds back too.

  Removing it is otherwise never destructive: the cost of being wrong is
  time on the next boot, not lost work, which is why it reports what it
  reclaims and why it is opt-in rather than part of ""--deep"".
end note

note right of CORE
  **Pure decision core.** ""BuildPlan"" performs no I/O:
  ""cmd/proveo"" gathers the inventory and executes. That
  is what makes the liveness rules unit-testable without
  Docker.

  **Liveness is the invariant.** A running container, or
  a network that still has endpoints, is left alone and
  reported in ""SkippedLive"" — a concurrent ""proveo run""
  must survive a clean. ""--force"" is the only override.
end note

note bottom of ST
  Wiping egress state is a **security** action, not just
  disk hygiene: a crashed docker-era run could leave the
  injected ""broker.env"" (the real provider key) on disk.
  Routine clean removes it. No run writes one since
  2026-10-16.
end note

note bottom of PH
  Deliberately excluded from both routine and ""--deep"":
  it is the user's durable session history, not run
  ephemera. Upstream sidecar bases (squid, ollama) are
  likewise left — shared and cheap to re-pull. See _spec/internal/proveohome/proveo-home-components.puml
end note
note bottom of CORE
  **The decision core is pure: an inventory in, a removal set out.** That is
  what lets the two tiers be asserted without Docker present.

  **"Live" protects the whole session.** HISTORY: when any of a docker-era
  session's egress containers was still running, its networks //and// its
  state directory were preserved. Now a session is live when its proveo
  process answers ""Signal(0)"" (""sessionAlive"" → ""Inventory.LiveSessions""),
  and its state dir — the sbx Kit and the policy log a live run still
  writes — is preserved. Anything skipped for that reason is reported rather than
  silently kept, so an operator who expected a reclaim learns why it did
  not happen.

  Routine covers per-run ephemera left by a crashed or killed run — egress
  session containers and networks, session state dirs, and
  ""proveo-dind-*"" sidecars from before that sidecar was retired
  (_spec/_paradigms/retire-dind.puml). Nothing starts one now, and the sweep
  is kept precisely for that reason: a ""--privileged"" container an older
  proveo left running is the last thing to strand on a host with nothing
  left that knows its name. The deeper tier is opt-in because it reaches
  images the next run would otherwise reuse.
end note


@enduml
